        en: 'This is chapter 4 construction section: turning the generative view into plain Python functions. The book builds its original LDA, QDA, and Naive Bayes classes on numpy arrays; we rebuild the same core with lists and loops so every step is visible: a Gaussian density for one class, then a full LDA classifier invoking Bayes rule, then a count model for Naive Bayes. All expected results are pre-computed and pinned in tests — your build either matches them or exposes itself.',
