          en: 'A book-level observation to keep while building: in one dimension, Gaussian Naive Bayes is mathematically identical to QDA — both are a mean and a variance per class. The naive assumption does nothing when there is a single feature; its value appears when features multiply and a product replaces a joint distribution. So in these exercises nb works on word counts (genuinely multiple features), not on a single Gaussian.',
