        en: 'This is QDA in its original dress: multiply the 0.5 prior by a Gaussian density using each class variance. At x = 4: density*prior is 0.0122 for class 0 and 0.0226 for class 1 — the wide class 1 wins, as seen in the first lesson. The same template serves all three exercises: density, then scores, then argmax. Change x to 5.0 in your local copy and watch the wide-class margin widen as the point moves farther out.',
